# 4.3.scenario.elimination.assay.plan.stone

## .what

sequence the ranked tests into an **ordered assay plan**, and state — for each test — **what each
result eliminates**. this is the map that collapses the superposition: run test, read result, drop
the scenarios it rules out, repeat.

## .inputs

- `4.2.scenario.elimination.assay.rank.yield.md` — the ranked tests

## .do

- order the tests (cheap high-power + catastrophic-branch first)
- for each test, write the result → elimination map ("fever present → keeps systemic branch; absent →
  lowers it"), so the driver knows exactly which scenarios each outcome drops
- name which scenarios **remain live** if every test comes back inconclusive (the irreducible set)

## .emit

into `4.3.scenario.elimination.assay.plan.yield.md` — the ordered plan + per-result elimination map.

## .done when

the tests are ordered, each carries a result→elimination map, and the irreducible-if-inconclusive set
is named.
